The com.google.gms.google-services plugin fails the build with
"File google-services.json is missing" unless a real one sits at
app/google-services.json.

To get yours:
  1. https://console.firebase.google.com -> your project (or create one)
  2. Project settings (gear icon) -> "Your apps" -> Add app -> Android
  3. Android package name: com.dormmate
     (the debug buildType adds ".debug", so ALSO register com.dormmate.debug,
      or you will get "No matching client found" when running a debug build)
  4. Download google-services.json
  5. Drop it at app/google-services.json  (same folder as app/build.gradle)
  6. Enable in the console: Authentication (Email/Password),
     Cloud Firestore, Storage, Cloud Messaging

Then delete this TEMPLATE file.
